# Verbatim evidence — APPEND these two lines to your own .gitattributes (K11).
#
# Captured command output is evidence: its bytes ARE the claim. Two of git's normal, helpful
# behaviours corrupt it silently.
#   -whitespace  the pre-commit whitespace rule (and `git apply --whitespace=fix`) rewrites
#                trailing spaces and tab/space runs — real characters of a captured terminal.
#   -text        disables CRLF/LF normalisation, which mangles output captured on another
#                platform and changes the file's hash without changing what you ran.
# Without both, an artifact you cite as "here is exactly what the command printed" is not
# exactly what the command printed, and nothing tells you.
#
# Adjust the path to wherever your evidence lives; the attributes are the load-bearing part.
docs/evidence/**   -whitespace -text
